{
  "chapter.0033EF722DDC4F60.title": "05 • Ender IO: Compact Automation",
  "task.4597FB3E4E49456D.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.7C4EF9DE3DEF3BA6.title": "Start here: Ender IO",
  "quest.7C4EF9DE3DEF3BA6.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.7C4EF9DE3DEF3BA6.quest_desc": [
    "Ender IO provides processing machines, alloys, compact conduit networks and soul-based automation. Its strength is fitting several transport systems into a small space while keeping filters and machine sides under control.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/enderio.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• Alloy Workshop",
    "• Conduit Systems",
    "• Souls & Spawners",
    "• Farming & Utilities",
    "",
    "Your route: machine parts and power -> alloys and crushing -> conduits -> automatic processing -> soul tools and farming -> a compact production cell.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.132F575EDD3C69DE.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.3E769EE8AD936310.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.3E769EE8AD936310.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.3E769EE8AD936310.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "task.41159FEA92B86C19.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2E87657515D476F3.title": "Read the machine chain",
  "quest.2E87657515D476F3.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.2E87657515D476F3.quest_desc": [
    "Ender IO's recipes and available machines differ across releases. This installed 8.2 version should be learned through its actual JEI categories.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Search @enderio in JEI. Inspect the Alloy Smelter, SAG Mill, chassis and capacitor recipes, then identify which starting resources your workshop can already produce.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not follow an old guide's machine name blindly. Use the exact item shown by this pack and inspect all recipe tabs."
  ],
  "task.3A5880F1DD16574C.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2F7775F6E4C7C850.title": "Power and a buffer",
  "quest.2F7775F6E4C7C850.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.2F7775F6E4C7C850.quest_desc": [
    "A capacitor bank stores FE and gives your processing machines a visible energy buffer.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Connect a Basic Capacitor Bank to an available FE source, configure its input/output faces and power one machine. Watch the stored energy while the machine processes.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Stored energy is not generation. If the bank drains steadily, improve supply or reduce simultaneous machine demand."
  ],
  "task.4EEE8D270E09E0C0.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.052DA5A01BF9913D.title": "Alloy Smelter",
  "quest.052DA5A01BF9913D.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.052DA5A01BF9913D.quest_desc": [
    "The Alloy Smelter combines materials into the alloys used throughout Ender IO.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Supply power and any capacitor required by the machine interface. Select an alloy recipe in JEI, insert the exact ingredients and collect the output.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "PROVE THE RECIPE: Install the capacitor required by the machine, supply FE, select an appropriate alloy/smelting mode and run one JEI recipe by hand. Keep an output slot free. Automation should reproduce this known working setup.",
    "",
    "SIDES: Use the machine's side configuration/Yeta Wrench and conduit connection settings together. The machine must expose the intended inventory on the face being used; a conduit set to insert cannot override a disabled machine input.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Check the machine's smelting mode and redstone control if it processes an unexpected recipe or stays idle."
  ],
  "quest.4D6BABA78A1A59FF.title": "Build an alloy shelf",
  "quest.4D6BABA78A1A59FF.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.4D6BABA78A1A59FF.quest_desc": [
    "Different alloys unlock different devices. Keeping a small sample of each useful tier makes the progression easier to see.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect Energetic, Pulsating, Redstone and Conductive Alloy uses. Make the alloy needed for your next machine or conduit rather than crafting every available metal at once.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Tag substitutions are recipe-specific. Verify the accepted ingredient before automating alloy production."
  ],
  "task.5A5012AC97C2692E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.519FCA5725322C0C.title": "SAG Mill processing",
  "quest.519FCA5725322C0C.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.519FCA5725322C0C.quest_desc": [
    "The SAG Mill handles crushing recipes and can provide different outputs from ordinary smelting.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Power the mill, inspect the desired recipe in JEI and process a small sample. Read the output amounts and any optional grinding-ball effects before supplying a bulk input.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A grinding ball is an optimization, not permission to assume every ore doubles. Check the displayed recipe and secondary outputs."
  ],
  "task.002F7773E819906D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5B861CA204819EB3.title": "Machine sides and slots",
  "quest.5B861CA204819EB3.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.5B861CA204819EB3.quest_desc": [
    "A machine can have power and ingredients nearby while still exposing the wrong input or output face.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the machine's side configuration. Set a clear input face and output route, then test each with an ordinary inventory before connecting a complex conduit bundle.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a chest at the output during testing. Visible intermediate results make it easier to diagnose where a stack stopped."
  ],
  "task.0945C5CE033D8D93.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.495FB0FFBFA9A604.title": "Item conduits",
  "quest.495FB0FFBFA9A604.quest_subtitle": "Conduit Systems",
  "quest.495FB0FFBFA9A604.quest_desc": [
    "Item conduits move resources between inventories using per-connection settings.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Connect two test chests with Item Conduits. Set the source connection to extract and the destination to insert, choose matching routing settings and check redstone behavior. Move a small stack.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "TWO CHESTS FIRST: Put a conduit connection on each chest. Configure the source connection for extraction and the destination for insertion on the same item-channel color. Enable extraction without a redstone signal for this first test, then transfer a few cobble.",
    "",
    "SHARED SPACE: Different conduit types can occupy one block space. Their settings are still independent: an item route does not power the machine. Add energy after the item route works, then verify both tabs.",
    "",
    "VERSION NOTE: This Ender IO version stores the conduit type as item data. The quest uses the actual Item Conduit variant rather than an empty generic conduit that has no useful type.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A connected cable is not an enabled extractor. Inspect both ends when nothing moves.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/enderio.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.5F5A18F91DDA818B.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7A32722C6F05946B.title": "Filter before expanding",
  "quest.7A32722C6F05946B.quest_subtitle": "Conduit Systems",
  "quest.7A32722C6F05946B.quest_desc": [
    "Filters stop a shared pipe from moving every item in a machine or storage chest.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Add an appropriate item filter at the relevant connection. Allow one test material, put a different material beside it and verify that only the intended stack moves.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use separate routing colors/channels where supported for unrelated flows. Keep inputs and finished outputs from feeding each other in a loop."
  ],
  "task.1BFCEB17B908586F.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.1958E66FB7A2F755.title": "Energy beside items",
  "quest.1958E66FB7A2F755.quest_subtitle": "Conduit Systems",
  "quest.1958E66FB7A2F755.quest_desc": [
    "Conduit bundles can combine different transport types in the same space, reducing cable clutter.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Add the installed energy conduit type to a short tested item-conduit route. Connect a machine, configure its power faces and verify both item movement and energy delivery.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A compact bundle still contains separate transport rules. Debug the energy route independently of the item route."
  ],
  "task.17F0BC12A9B40C4D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0847046BBB793BC3.title": "Fluids and dedicated lines",
  "quest.0847046BBB793BC3.quest_subtitle": "Conduit Systems",
  "quest.0847046BBB793BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Fluid routing has its own tanks, accepted fluids and extraction settings. Mixing incompatible fluids can stall processing.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Use the fluid conduit type suited to your needs. Move one ordinary fluid between two tanks and verify the amount and direction before connecting an Ender IO fluid machine.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a single-fluid test network first. Check whether the chosen conduit tier supports the behavior you want."
  ],
  "task.307020DCB30DD339.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.36DB0C7DDC0204CC.title": "Capacitors and throughput",
  "quest.36DB0C7DDC0204CC.quest_subtitle": "Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.36DB0C7DDC0204CC.quest_desc": [
    "Machine capacitors and upgrades can change performance and energy demand. Faster operation is useful only when inputs and power keep up.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare the machine's supported capacitor options in JEI and its GUI. Upgrade one machine, run the same small recipe batch and compare its energy use and completion time.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Loot capacitors can have different properties. Read their information rather than treating every capacitor as an identical tier."
  ],
  "task.232E974278F09CD3.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.1CF4535FA329C06F.title": "Project: automated alloy",
  "quest.1CF4535FA329C06F.quest_subtitle": "Conduit Systems",
  "quest.1CF4535FA329C06F.quest_desc": [
    "A repeatable alloy setup combines controlled ingredients, a powered smelter and a reliable output route.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Feed one tested alloy recipe from a dedicated input chest and return its output to a separate chest or RS. Run several batches and confirm ingredients do not overfill unintended slots.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "For RS, encode the real input/output quantities as a processing pattern. Do not let an independent stock system endlessly refill the same machine input."
  ],
  "task.2DD0CAAAE0AA3A72.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.18CB692F90461B2E.title": "Capture a sample soul",
  "quest.18CB692F90461B2E.quest_subtitle": "Souls & Spawners",
  "quest.18CB692F90461B2E.quest_desc": [
    "Soul Vials carry eligible creatures for Ender IO's soul-based recipes. This is different from the numeric Souls resource in Industrial Foregoing.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Craft a Soul Vial, read its tooltip and inspect recipes that use captured entities. Choose an eligible ordinary creature and test the capture interaction.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Inspect the filled vial's entity information before using it. Different recipes require different creatures."
  ],
  "task.05E2A68F2E0D9E42.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.50F2AAA0133514C2.title": "The Soul Binder",
  "quest.50F2AAA0133514C2.quest_subtitle": "Souls & Spawners",
  "quest.50F2AAA0133514C2.quest_desc": [
    "The Soul Binder combines a captured soul with ingredients to produce specialized components.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect a Soul Binder recipe in JEI, including its entity and XP requirements. Supply the machine's needs and complete one recipe that supports your next device.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If progress does not begin, check entity type, ingredients, energy, capacitor and required experience separately."
  ],
  "task.52911EDE9F2DC0A1.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.69E2304783FD1AF7.title": "Powered spawning",
  "quest.69E2304783FD1AF7.quest_subtitle": "Souls & Spawners",
  "quest.69E2304783FD1AF7.quest_desc": [
    "A Powered Spawner is a controllable mob-production system with substantial power and containment needs.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Follow the installed recipe path for configuring the desired mob. Build a contained test chamber, provide a stop control, and run a short spawning test only after you have a collection/handling plan.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "SPAWNER CHAIN: Capture the intended mob in a Soul Vial, inspect the Soul Binder recipe for changing a broken spawner, supply its FE/XP requirements, then follow the installed recipe for the Powered Spawner. A plain empty Soul Vial is only a tool, not a configured mob source.",
    "",
    "BEFORE ENABLE: Build an enclosure with a collection method, a stop signal and enough output storage. Start at low throughput. A faster capacitor can raise the power demand beyond what the same supply handled at the previous tier.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Check eligible mobs and space conditions. Start with an ordinary target and keep the farm disabled while editing it."
  ],
  "task.1E12761C0F40FCC5.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3F0678911B3AD0EC.title": "Experience handling",
  "quest.3F0678911B3AD0EC.quest_subtitle": "Souls & Spawners",
  "quest.3F0678911B3AD0EC.quest_desc": [
    "An XP Obelisk provides a dedicated experience buffer for your own use and compatible workflows.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place the obelisk, inspect deposit/withdraw controls and test with a small amount of experience. Identify the XP form accepted by any connected machine before adding pipes.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "XP Juice, ordinary fluid and unrelated experience resources are not automatically interchangeable."
  ],
  "task.1FE56A231F891D03.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.7DE59D4E25BF5649.title": "A Farming Station",
  "quest.7DE59D4E25BF5649.quest_subtitle": "Farming & Utilities",
  "quest.7DE59D4E25BF5649.quest_desc": [
    "The Farming Station can automate supported plants when supplied with the required tools, power and inventory space.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Place it beside a small suitable growing area. Provide the requested tools and seeds/saplings, configure the farm, and watch a complete harvest and replant cycle.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Reserve seeds or saplings for replanting and leave output capacity. A full inventory can look like a broken farm."
  ],
  "task.36B12A9E61626741.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0173532A28D86EA6.title": "Choose a specialist device",
  "quest.0173532A28D86EA6.quest_subtitle": "Farming & Utilities",
  "quest.0173532A28D86EA6.quest_desc": [
    "Ender IO also offers utility devices such as chargers, tanks, enchanting and obelisks. These should solve a need in your base.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the Enchanter, Wired Charger and available obelisks in JEI. Choose one useful device, read its requirements and prove its function with a small test.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Skip devices you do not need yet. The goal is understanding their role, not crafting every item in the mod."
  ],
  "task.31B2DD453A0061F3.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.114C498123F7AD6F.title": "Project: compact workshop",
  "quest.114C498123F7AD6F.quest_subtitle": "Conduit Systems",
  "quest.114C498123F7AD6F.quest_desc": [
    "A good compact system remains understandable after the cables are hidden.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Combine your tested alloy or crushing setup with item return, power buffering and a visible stop control. Label its inputs and outputs, then demonstrate how you diagnose a missing-input or power problem.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep machine access faces reachable. Hide conduits only after filters, directions and recovery behavior are proven."
  ],
  "task.3C2392B71A064B57.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.15DA28DCBC196B41.title": "The conduit workshop starts here",
  "quest.15DA28DCBC196B41.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.15DA28DCBC196B41.quest_desc": [
    "Conduit Binder is a recurring ingredient in Ender IO transport. Making a small stock now keeps you from stopping the machine lesson for another crafting trip.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect Binder Composite and Conduit Binder in JEI, make a small batch of the composite and process it through the displayed route. Collect 16 binder and reserve part of it for the first item and energy lines.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use the recipe shown in this pack. Do not assume a familiar-looking gravel/clay mixture has the same quantities as an older version."
  ],
  "task.6FF245242EBAC9D6.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.495F6D63B901B423.title": "Start the alloy ladder",
  "quest.495F6D63B901B423.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.495F6D63B901B423.quest_desc": [
    "Conductive Alloy is a useful early output for the transport and power branch. A stable alloy recipe proves that the smelter receives the correct ingredients and energy.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Run the JEI recipe by hand and collect eight ingots. Then supply exactly one recipe batch through your intended input face and confirm that the result is the same.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Wrong result? Check machine mode and recipe competition before blaming the conduit. Keep unrelated smeltable ingredients out of the first trial."
  ],
  "task.17079987F1593F28.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.28D7FBF6F7D5296E.title": "Make a later alloy on demand",
  "quest.28D7FBF6F7D5296E.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.28D7FBF6F7D5296E.quest_desc": [
    "Later alloys depend on earlier alloy production. Treat this as a short chain with an intermediate buffer, rather than an unlabelled chest full of every ingredient.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Pin the Vibrant Alloy recipe and trace each ingredient back one step in JEI. Produce eight ingots, then reserve the earlier alloy needed to repeat the batch.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If an earlier alloy is also exported to storage or the market, keep a reserve so the next machine in the chain does not starve."
  ],
  "task.2306ED35505819A5.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.308340B2013E9493.title": "A processing recipe, measured",
  "quest.308340B2013E9493.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.308340B2013E9493.quest_desc": [
    "SAG Mill recipes can have multiple outputs and recipe-specific modifiers. Automation must allow room for byproducts as well as the material you wanted.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose one inexpensive JEI recipe, record the input amount and expected main output, then run a short batch. Inspect every resulting slot before connecting output extraction.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Do not promise a probabilistic bonus as a guaranteed RS processing output. Encode only an output the machine can reliably return."
  ],
  "task.6FEA6F97FDA9E7EC.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.5DAA7033E72D7051.title": "Buffer the demand spikes",
  "quest.5DAA7033E72D7051.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Alloy Workshop",
  "quest.5DAA7033E72D7051.quest_desc": [
    "A larger capacitor bank stores energy between bursts of work. It does not increase generation by itself, and fast machines can still empty it.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare stored FE with the workshop idle and with two machines running. Add a suitable bank when the measured buffer is too small, then watch whether it refills after the batch.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If it never recovers, generation is below average demand. More storage only delays the eventual stop."
  ],
  "task.489302E66608074B.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3BFAF61D9C21CB29.title": "Separate experience from items",
  "quest.3BFAF61D9C21CB29.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Souls & Spawners",
  "quest.3BFAF61D9C21CB29.quest_desc": [
    "The XP Obelisk is an experience buffer. It can support an XP workflow, but item transport and XP transfer remain different resources.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Deposit a small known amount using the obelisk interface, retrieve part of it and compare the displayed totals. Only then connect a supported automation route used by your Soul Binder setup.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep the first XP experiment reversible. A machine waiting for experience can have plenty of FE and all its item ingredients."
  ]
}
